Instructions to build an OpenSmalltalk-VM for the QNX 8.0 microkernel.

It is assumed the build system is x86 Linux and target is Raspberry Pi 4 QNX.

There is no requirement for Visual Studio, but you will need the free
QNX licence and Software Development Platform available from:
   https://qnx.com/getqnx

Docs at:
   https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/qnxeverywhere/index.html

The basic differences from a Linux build are that
  [A] OpenSmalltalk-VM is cross compiled [x86 build -> aarch64 runtime]
  [B] QNX includes and libraries are required

Basic Steps:
 [0] Get QNX SDP [url above]
 [1] Get OpenSmalltalk-VM
   cd $HOME
   ## Fixme: release to Opensmalltalk/OpenSmalltalk-VM
   git clone --filter=blob:none https://github.com/KenDickey/opensmalltalk-vm
 [2] Build it
   cd opensmalltalk-vm/building/qnx64ARMv8/squeak.stack.spur/build
   ./mvm
   #@@@ CURRENT IS BROKEN - built & tested with hand work; scp to rpi4 target.
 [3] Copy VM files to QNX Target
 [4] Copy Smalltalk image, changes, sources files to QNX target [no git available]
 [5] Playtime!


